t": "The worst move of GPT-6.1 Sol's game. Black stood level at +0.1, and B7 dropped the lead to -19.8, a loss of 19.9 points. The engine's choice was B8."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "Black kept crawling down the B-file with B2 (19.8 points lost), after B3 at move 35 lost 13.8, while the 20k answered along the A-file. Each exchange left Black behind: after B2 the lead stood at -23.6."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "The 20k's A1 was its worst move, losing 23.8 points and lifting Black's lead from -23.7 to +0.0. After this the game was level, and the engine called the remaining play even for the rest of the endgame, which led to the draw."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran (the `inspect` function in game-191-inspector.js, the per-move `audit` calls, the `play` wrapper, and the postgame replay) only parses the current board, lists chains, liberties and empty regions, applies one named move to report captures and legality, replays the actual record to check it, and writes notes and SGF files. It never loops over candidate moves or looks ahead; the moves and the lines of play were chosen by hand.", "stop": false}}